findings.root_cause:
Confirmed: native.rs:2298-2315 builds SourceConventionSlots from convention.args and return_register() only. with_variadic_tail_on_stack is only set in the test at stack.rs:616.
placed_prefix (native.rs:1543-1597) uses separate integer and float counters. That is wrong for:
- Win64 (positional: the 2nd parameter, if double, is XMM1, and its RDX slot is consumed);
- ARM32 AAPCS (64-bit values in even-aligned register pairs; armhf VFP back-filling);
- RISC-V (FP operands spill to integer registers once the FP registers are exhausted);
- x86-64 long double (MEMORY class on the stack; parse gives Float and it would take an XMM).
The result side is one register: no RAX:RDX pair for __int128 or two-eightbyte structs, no XMM0:XMM1, no ST0, no AArch64 HFA V0-V3.
